# Project Theme & Visual Language
- Desktop theme is **"Broadcast"** (NFL.com-inspired): near-white background, navy primary chrome, red accents. Tokens live in `src/styles.css` `:root` (`--background`, `--primary`, `--accent`, position colors `--pos-*`, etc.).
- Maintain the existing light aesthetic; do not apply terminal-style, purple-glow, or generic AI dashboard themes to components.
- Fonts: **Archivo** (`--font-sans`) for body; **Barlow Condensed** (`--font-display`) for titles via the `display-title` utility (uppercase, tracking). Loaded from `__root.tsx`.
- Content width: `max-w-shell` (90rem). Page shells typically use `main.mx-auto.w-full.max-w-shell.px-3.pb-16.pt-6`.
- Page titles: `h1.display-title.text-3xl.text-slate-900` with the distinctive second word in `text-primary` when it fits (e.g. Fantasy Points **Allowed**).
- The only dark-themed desktop exception is the Hall of Fame page (`hof.tsx`: almost black / zinc-950, amber accents).
- Mobile `/m/*` routes use separate `.mobile-theme-light` / `.mobile-theme-dark` tokens — do not mix those into desktop research/playbook pages.
- Prefer theme tokens / existing slate-blue utility patterns already used on research boards; do not invent a new color system per page.

# Shared UI & Chrome Rules
- When creating new pages or views, always preserve and wrap them in the existing layout structure to retain the top navbar (`SiteNav`) and live ticker (`ScoreTicker`) from `__root.tsx`. Skip both only on `/m` mobile routes (already handled in root).
- League-scoped tools (Playbook, Trade, Waiver, Top Available, etc.) wrap with `PlaybookShell` (`section`: `playbook` | `trade` | `waiver`; `wide` for Trade Desk). Do not rebuild guest/no-league gates — `PlaybookShell` + `AccessGate` + `PlaybookSubNav` own that.
- Do not add icons next to descriptions in dropdown navigation layouts (Research menu, Playbook subnav, etc.).
- In the profile dropdown, place **Account** at the top of the list. Never shrink the navbar profile circle (`size-8` / `h-8 w-8`).
- Maintain clean blue account-style text-only button designs. Strictly no bracket symbols [] or emojis in buttons or main section headers.
- Open players via `PlayerModalHost` ref (`open(id)`), not one-off modal state per page.
- League-scoped titles should include `ActiveLeagueLabel` when the tool depends on the synced league.
- Injuries: use `resolveInjuryStatus` / `injuryMicroBadge` from `sandbox-rosters` — do not invent ad-hoc status strings.
- Sandbox mode (`ActiveLeagueContext.sandboxMode`) unlocks Trade Desk / mock rosters without a synced league — preserve that behavior; do not remove the exit-to-prior-league path.
- Player brain hydration (`usePlayerBrain` / `hydratePlayerBrain`) is silent and non-blocking — do not gate UI on it.

# Research Page & Player Table Design
# New research / leaderboard / projection boards must match existing pages
# (fantasy-points-allowed, fantasy-leaders, matchups-guide, sos-analysis, red-zone-stats,
# most-targeted-players, trade-market-values, weekly/season-projections, top-available).

- Reuse `src/components/research/*`: `SortHeader` (`SortHeaderButton`, `nextSortState`, `PLAYER_LIST_*` classes), `ScoringFormatSelect` + `useResearchScoringFormat`, `ValueTrendCell`, `ProjectionListRow` / `PROJECTION_OWNERSHIP_META`, `projectionStatColumns`, `statRanks`.
- Sort cycle is 3-click via `nextSortState`: activate → flip direction → clear.
- Grouped stat tables: two header rows (`PLAYER_LIST_GROUP_HEADER_ROW` + `PLAYER_LIST_COL_HEADER_ROW`); leave Rk/Player group cells blank (no “Players” label). Single-row boards use `PLAYER_LIST_HEADER_ROW`.
- Table chrome: wrap the board in `overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm` with an inner `overflow-x-auto`. Research boards use this white sheet — do not invent a new card/dashboard layout.
- Scoring format: default from the synced league via `useResearchScoringFormat`, fallback `"half"`; change filters with `startTransition`. Search text should use `useDeferredValue` when filtering large lists.
- Position filter chips: active `border-blue-600 bg-blue-600 text-white`; inactive white / `text-blue-700`.
- UI label for defense position is **DST** (internal pos remains `DEF`).
- Market value columns: `ValueTrendCell` + `scaleValue`; column label is **Value/Trend** (never a bare `$` header).
- Research routes, Trade Desk (`/trade`), and The Wire (`/waiver`): `ssr: false` (SSR catalog loaders burn Fluid Active CPU).
- Remount league-dependent boards with `key={activeLeagueId ?? "none"}` when the active league changes.
- Prefer CDN research helpers (`research-cdn`) with `staleTime: RESEARCH_CLIENT_STALE_MS` and `placeholderData: (prev) => prev` so format toggles do not flash empty.

# Data & AI Logic Constraints
- Never suggest dropping essential starting positions or players that would leave a roster vacancy (such as dropping a solo defense).
- Use explicit text explanations for component placements instead of referencing user-provided images.
- Use the text labels "Value/Trend" for player metrics instead of a standard dollar sign ($).

# Free-Tier Performance & Limit Guardrails (Vercel Fluid / TiDB / visitor IPs)
# One solo tester previously burned >50% of monthly Fluid Active CPU. Keep these
# rules when adding features — do not reintroduce Fluid waterfalls or dump load
# onto TiDB RUs, GitHub raw, or visitor Sleeper/ESPN rate limits.

## Default data path (prefer in this order)
1. Browser → public APIs with IndexedDB (`getCached` in `sleeper-cache`, helpers in `sleeper-client`, `sleeper-rosters-client`, `sleeper-league-sync-client`, `scoring-client`, `sleeper-trending`).
2. Browser → **GitHub `snap-cdn` branch** via `VITE_SNAP_CDN_BASE` / `r2-public.ts` (research + public snap JSON; no Fluid). Actions workflow **Publish Snap CDN** force-pushes the orphan branch.
3. Browser → `/api/data/research/*` (`research-cdn`, TiDB SELECT-only), `/api/data/league/$id` (`league-matchups-cdn`), `/api/data/players-export`. Browse `/api/data/snap/*` soft-empties — **no compute** (see below).
4. Fluid `createServerFn` only for credentials/secrets/writes (ESPN s2/swid, Yahoo OAuth, league sync writes, account delete) or true last-resort misses in **dev**.

## GitHub snap-cdn (no-card public JSON)
- Client helpers in `research-cdn` / `snap-cdn` call `r2Url(...)` first (`VITE_SNAP_CDN_BASE`, legacy alias `VITE_R2_PUBLIC_BASE`).
- Object keys: `R2_RESEARCH_KEYS` / `R2_SNAP_KEYS` in `r2-public.ts` (includes `injury-wire.json`).
- **Never promote / redeploy the `snap-cdn` branch on Vercel** — it is JSON-only and will 404 Production. `vercel.json` sets `git.deploymentEnabled.snap-cdn: false`.
- Warm shared snaps with Actions → **Publish Snap CDN** (uses `CRON_SECRET` so `/api/data/snap/*` may compute for the publish fetch only).

## Client-first caching without burning visitor IPs
- Prefer client/public fetches **and** snap-cdn / CDN, but never unbounded fan-out from the browser.
- Always wrap public Sleeper (and similar) fetches in `getCached(key, ttlMs, fetcher)` so IndexedDB/localStorage + in-flight dedupe share one download per visitor.
- Cap concurrency when a week/player fan-out is unavoidable (existing pattern: projection weeks `PROJ_WEEK_CONCURRENCY = 2` in `sleeper-client`; do not raise without cause). Prefer shared week bundles over per-player downloads.
- Reuse shared React Query keys instead of inventing parallel caches: `["players-catalog"]`, `["player", id, "client-v1"]`, `["nfl-state", …]`, `["league-scoring", "v5", …]`, `["league-rosters", connectionId]`, `["league-matchups-cdn-all", …]`, `["injury-reports"]`, `["injury-wire", limit]`, `["trade-value-basis"]`, `["fantasy-news-feed", limit]`, etc.
- Global RQ defaults (`router.tsx`): `staleTime` 5m, `gcTime` 30m, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false`, `refetchIntervalInBackground: false` — do not override these to be more aggressive for heavy queries.
- Soft-empty / stale-on-error for public reads — do not retry storms on 429; one polite backoff then stop (see `sleeper-client`).
- ESPN athlete/news feeds are especially ban-prone: batch via snaps (`fetchSnapFantasyNews`, `fetchSnapRosterNews`, injury snaps) — never N concurrent Fluid or browser ESPN calls per visible row.
- When data is identical for every visitor, publish to **snap-cdn** (and/or cron → TiDB for research SELECTs) so each client hits GitHub/edge once, not Fluid.

## Never do these (regressions we already fixed)
- Do not call Fluid `createServerFn` for public Sleeper reads (state, projections, stats, game logs, bio, next game, trending, Sleeper rosters/scoring when league id is known).
- Do not fan out N Fluid calls per page (e.g. one `getConnectionMatchups` / `getPlayerNews` per week or per visible row). Use one CDN/all-weeks fetch or one shared snap.
- Do not add `refetchOnWindowFocus: true` for heavy Sleeper/projection queries — IndexedDB TTL owns freshness.
- Do not poll while the tab is hidden. Use `visibleRefetchInterval` / `isPageVisible` from `page-visibility.ts`, and keep `refetchIntervalInBackground: false`.
- Do not fall back to Fluid in **production** when research/snap-cdn / `/api/data/*` misses — soft-empty instead (`allowFluidFallback` only when `import.meta.env.DEV`). Align new helpers with `research-cdn` / `snap-cdn`.
- Do not let browse `/api/data/snap/*` **compute** on miss — soft-empty unless `authorizeCronRequest` (Publish Snap CDN / Vercel cron with `CRON_SECRET`). Research `/api/data/research/*` stays TiDB SELECT-only (`allowCompute` only from research cron).
- Do not load full career game-log years on player popup open — use `fetchGameLogsClient(..., { includeCareer: false })` until Game Logs needs career.
- Do not re-download week projection bundles for ATP injuries — reuse `weekProjectionBundle` / live-injury overlay in `sleeper-client`.
- Do not bypass shared roster loaders: use `fetchLeagueRostersForConnection` (Sleeper client-first) for any `["league-rosters", …]` queryFn (Global Search, fantasy team name, playbook).
- Do not use playbook dashboard history via N× Fluid matchups — use `fetchLeagueAllMatchupsCdn` (same key as analytics).
- Do not wire Top Available / list headlines through N× `getPlayerNews` — use `fetchSnapFantasyNews` (or another single snap).
- Do not call `getRosterNews` Fluid directly from UI — use `fetchSnapRosterNews`.
- Do not call trade basis / injury reports / injury wire / fantasy news / trade market / Sleeper ROS / slot ranks via Fluid first — use the matching `fetchSnap*` helper in `snap-cdn.ts` (snap-cdn branch first).
- Do not call research aggregates (FPA, SOS, leaders, red zone, targets, ATP, matchups guide) via Fluid first — use `research-cdn` helpers (snap-cdn branch first).
- Do not assemble player detail via Fluid `getPlayerDetail` when catalog is warm — use `fetchPlayerDetailClient`.
- Do not call Fluid `getUserLeagues` / `getLeagueSync` for War Room / Draft — use `fetchUserLeaguesPreferred` / `fetchLeagueSyncPreferred` (`sleeper-league-sync-client`).
- Do not call Fluid `getConnectionSync` for public Sleeper draft setup — use `fetchConnectionSyncPreferred` (`sleeper-sync-client`).
- Do not stamp homepage Injury Wire `published` from ESPN designation `date` when the copy is RotoWire — use the RotoWire/Sleeper news time; show the top N by that real news time (`loadInjuryWire`).
- Do not shorten CDN TTLs or remove `processMemo` coalescing on TiDB-backed **research/league** data routes without a clear freshness need (RU burn).
- Do not lower league sync cooldown below the intentional long window (cron owns frequent refresh; page loads only top up stale sessions).
- Do not call Fluid `deltaSyncLeague` on Sleeper browse page loads — GitHub Actions → `/api/cron/league-delta-sync` (+ daily `fillSeason`) owns the warm; browsers read CDN/client.
- Do not call Fluid `getConnectionStandings` for public Sleeper leagues — use `fetchSleeperStandingsClient` (`sleeper-standings-client`).
- Do not call Fluid `getConnectionMeta` / `getConnectionSettings` / `getConnectionTransactions` / `getConnectionTransactionLog` for Sleeper — use `sleeper-meta-client`, `league-settings-fetch`, `league-activity-fetch`.
- Do not call Fluid `getHallOfFame` — use `loadHallOfFame` (browser → Supabase anon).
- Do not fall back to Fluid `getPlayerDetail` in production when the catalog client misses — soft-empty instead.
- Do not call Fluid `getPickupResults` for Sleeper — use `fetchPickupResultsPreferred` (`pickup-results-client`).
- Do not move heavy work onto GitHub raw/nflverse downloads on the **app request** path (prefer cron → TiDB / Publish Snap CDN). Serving published JSON from the `snap-cdn` branch is intentional.
- Keep Actions warm jobs lean: `league-delta-sync.yml` (gameday **hourly**, daily fillSeason), `league-planning-snaps.yml` (once daily + Tue, small limit), `research-aggregates.yml` (GH owns research warm — no duplicate Vercel daily), `publish-snap-cdn.yml`. Do not reintroduce per-visitor Fluid or 30m gameday delta storms.

## When Fluid is allowed
- ESPN/Yahoo paths that require `s2` / `swid` / OAuth tokens.
- League sync writes: `deltaSyncLeague`, `forceClearAndReSyncLeague`, cron host→TiDB upserts.
- Admin / account / secret-gated operations.
- Cron-authenticated snap **compute** for Publish Snap CDN / planning warm (`CRON_SECRET` / `x-vercel-cron`). Anonymous browse must soft-empty.
- Research/league `/api/data/*` TiDB SELECT origins (shared; not per-visitor `createServerFn`).
- Dev-only Fluid fallback when local snaps are cold.

## When adding a new data surface
- Ask: can the browser fetch this publicly with `getCached` (and a concurrency cap if fan-out is needed)?
- If shared across visitors: publish via **Publish Snap CDN** (`r2-public` keys + `research-cdn` / `snap-cdn` client) and/or TiDB research SELECT routes; wire soft-empty in prod. Do not rely on anonymous `/api/data/snap/*` compute-on-miss.
- If league-scoped synced data: prefer `/api/data/league/$id` CDN (TiDB) over Fluid host pulls; Fluid refresh only when snap is cold/stale **and** the tab is visible (see `league-matchups-cdn`).
- If credentials required: keep Fluid, but cache aggressively client-side and avoid polling when hidden.
- Never “fix” Fluid burn by blasting TiDB on every page load without CDN/`processMemo`, or by unbounded concurrent Sleeper/ESPN calls from the browser.

## Key modules to reuse (do not reinvent)
- `src/lib/page-visibility.ts` — pause polls when hidden
- `src/lib/sleeper-cache.ts` / `sleeper-client.ts` / `sleeper-rosters-client.ts` / `sleeper-standings-client.ts` / `sleeper-meta-client.ts` / `sleeper-settings-client.ts` / `sleeper-activity-client.ts` / `sleeper-league-sync-client.ts` / `sleeper-sync-client.ts` / `scoring-client.ts` / `sleeper-trending.ts`
- `src/lib/r2-public.ts` / `research-cdn.ts` / `snap-cdn.ts` / `league-matchups-cdn.ts` / `league-rosters-fetch.ts` / `league-settings-fetch.ts` / `league-activity-fetch.ts`
- `src/lib/player-detail-client.ts` / `sos-from-board.ts` / `players-catalog.ts`
- `src/lib/process-memo.ts` / `cron-auth.server.ts` / `api-cache.ts` (`dataCacheControl`, `leagueHistoryCacheControl`, `researchCacheControl`, `warehouseCacheControl`)
- `src/components/research/*`, `PlaybookShell`, `PlayerModalHost`, `ActiveLeagueLabel`
- Routes: `api/data/research.$kind.ts`, `api/data/snap.$kind.ts`, `api/data/league.$id.ts`, `api/data/players-export.ts`
- Docs: `docs/snap-cdn-setup.md`

# Strict Schema Utilization Instructions
- Always use these exact active tables and property data types when writing TypeScript functions, UI layout components, or custom Supabase mutations.
- The table `public.user_roles` has been completely dropped from the database schema cache. Never generate code targeting it.
- Admin privilege checks must read `profiles.role` and treat a value that strictly equals `admin` as admin access.

